what:
observe-explore (the explorer's daemon side, crate blaze-explore; design docs/v2/plan/lanes/observe/explore.md): root Cargo.toml [workspace.dependencies], versions checked against crates.io today (wtransport 0.7.2 is the latest, 2026-08-11; rcgen 0.14.10 the latest, 2026-08-28; both sources read in ~/.cargo/registry):

# The explorer's transport (crates/blaze-explore): HTTP/3 WebTransport on 127.0.0.1 with a
# self-signed certificate the page pins by hash. `ring` is the crypto rustls already uses here;
# no `self-signed` (rcgen is called directly, so its validity comes from a clock blaze passes).
wtransport = { version = "0.7.2", default-features = false, features = ["ring"] }
# The explorer's ECDSA P-256 certificate, made at start and rotated before it expires.
rcgen = { version = "0.14.10", default-features = false, features = ["ring"] }

and in the path-dependency block (beside blaze-profile; blaze-web is a member but not listed yet):
blaze-explore = { path = "crates/blaze-explore" }
blaze-web = { path = "crates/blaze-web" }

Cargo.lock regenerated (wtransport pulls quinn 0.11, wtransport-proto 0.7.2, x509-parser 0.18, sha2 0.11, socket2 0.6, url, pem; rcgen pulls yasna and time 0.3, already in the lock through other crates or new). Nothing uses these until crates/blaze-explore lands; I move it in only after this lands. arrow-array/arrow-ipc/arrow-schema come from 01412.
